Copy this directory's `settings.json.example` to `settings.json` to
pre-approve the common Bash commands the Arena Starter Kit runs
through Claude Code. This removes the first-time permission prompts
that fresh agents trigger when they hit an unfamiliar repo.

    cp .claude/settings.json.example .claude/settings.json

`.claude/settings.json` is git-ignored — your personal copy never gets
committed back. The `.example` file IS committed and stays in sync
with the commands the kit runs.

JSON does not support comments, which is why this note lives in a
sibling file rather than inside the JSON itself.

Other agents (Codex CLI, Cursor, Aider, etc.) have their own trust
mechanisms — see AGENTS.md "First-run permissions" for one-paragraph
pointers per agent. In all cases the answer is the same: approve when
prompted on first run; it's one-time.
